# Skills, and changes to CI, the skill publishing check, its rule data and its
# tests, need approval from a code owner. A pull request runs its own copy of
# each check, and the tests run in the same job before the check, so without
# this a pull request could edit a check to pass. The root .gitattributes is
# owned too, because it can change how the published skills are archived.
# Until the repository has a team for skill maintainers, the admins own all of
# them.
#
# This takes effect once branch protection turns on "Require review from Code
# Owners" for main.
/skills/ @aws/tools-for-devops-agent-admins
/.github/ @aws/tools-for-devops-agent-admins
/.gitattributes @aws/tools-for-devops-agent-admins
/tests/ @aws/tools-for-devops-agent-admins

# Connector definitions and connectors/releases.yaml, the version production
# serves. Until the repository has a team for connector maintainers, the admins
# own them.
/connectors/ @aws/tools-for-devops-agent-admins
